/Author (Wenxin Li) /CreationDate (D:20260506160806+00'00') /Creator (reportlab) /Keywords (Coordination Knowledge Substrate, CKS, anti-pattern, external tool state, system of record, source of truth, substrate, hybrid composition, Pattern A consultation, Pattern C separate concern, tool-agnosticism, vendor lock-in, integration architecture, AI coordination, human-governed, defensive publication) /ModDate (D:20260506160806+00'00') /Producer (ReportLab PDF Library - \(opensource\)) 
  /Subject (A standalone formalization of the CKS anti-pattern in which state held in external integrated systems \(third-party SaaS applications, external databases, integration platforms, external API services, external knowledge stores, external vector databases\) operates as authoritative for coordination questions, violating A1.08 \(substrate as source of truth\) and A1.16 \(hybrid systems composition\) simultaneously, with A1.05 tool-agnosticism extended-violated through vendor coupling.) /Title (Anti-Pattern: External Tool State Treated as Authoritative \204 Standalone Formalization of the Failure Mode Where State in External Integrated Systems Operates as Authoritative for Coordination Questions, Violating Substrate-as-Source-of-Truth and Hybrid Composition Architecture in CKS) /Trapped /False
>>
endobj
